# Workers Static Assets reads this file and doesn't serve it. It applies only
# to static assets, never to what the Worker renders.
#
# Everything the build writes under /assets/ has a content hash in its name, so
# a changed file gets a new address and the old one can be kept for a year with
# no revalidation. A cached font is then used with no request at all, which
# matters because font-display: optional (src/styles/fonts.css) never swaps in
# a font that misses the first paint. Never widen this rule to a file without
# a hash in its name: browsers would keep a stale copy for a year.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
